#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_beta_regularized

#% text
# `inverse_beta_regularized(s, a, b)` gives the `x` with `beta_regularized(x, a, b) = s`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For `a, b > 0` and `0 <= s <= 1` there is one solution in `[0, 1]`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% item
# `inverse_beta_regularized` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_beta_regularized(0.5, 2.0, 3.0)
#% output
#= 0.38572756813238956

#% cell
inverse_beta_regularized(0.5, 1.0, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.5

#% cell
inverse_beta_regularized(0.1, 0.5, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.024471741852423217

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The median of the beta distribution with parameters 2 and 5:

#% cell
inverse_beta_regularized(0.5, 2.0, 5.0)
#% output
#= 0.26444998329565994

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `beta_regularized` undoes it:

#% cell
beta_regularized(inverse_beta_regularized(0.3, 4.0, 2.0), 4.0, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.3

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `beta_regularized`, `beta`, `inverse_gamma_regularized`, `beta_distribution`
